<!DOCTYPE qhelp PUBLIC "-//Semmle//qhelp//EN" "qhelp.dtd">
<qhelp>
<overview>
<p>This opt-in query reports Java <code>NewClassExpr</code> and
<code>ArrayCreationExpr</code> nodes syntactically contained in a loop, with the
allocation and loop in the same enclosing callable. Each allocation is reported
once, including when several nested loops contain it.</p>
<p>Containment includes loop bodies and headers. A basic-for initializer or an
enhanced-for iterable expression can run once when a loop is entered; its presence
here does not mean it runs on every iteration. Unreachable or rarely executed code
can also be reported.</p>
<p>An allocation inside a lambda, local-class method or anonymous-class method is
not attributed to a loop in an enclosing callable. A loop inside that deferred
body can still produce its own findings. The explicit allocation of an anonymous
object in the outer loop is included. Implicit functional-object creation for
lambdas and method references is excluded.</p>
</overview>
<recommendation>
<p>Treat each result as a review candidate. Establish execution frequency,
allocation rate and application impact through measurement before proposing a
change. Moving or reusing an object can change identity, state, lifetime,
exceptions and concurrency behavior; this syntactic query does not prove that any
such change is safe. It neither tracks allocations through callees nor models
runtime optimization.</p>
</recommendation>
</qhelp>
